# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# TypeScript incremental build cache (emitted by `tsc -b` / the editor's TS server)
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vendored @freshon/api SDK — its compiled dist MUST be tracked so it ships
# with the standalone/subtree clone (the `dist` rule above would otherwise drop it).
!vendor/freshon-api/dist/
!vendor/freshon-api/dist/**

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
.env.*
.env
src-tauri/gen/android/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# In-tree Tauri plugin build output — Rust + Android. Source is tracked; these
# are regenerated by `cargo`/`gradle`/`tauri android` and must never be committed
# (a stray `git add` on the plugin dir otherwise stages tens of thousands of files).
src-tauri/plugins/*/target/
src-tauri/plugins/*/android/build/
src-tauri/plugins/*/android/.tauri/
src-tauri/plugins/*/android/.gradle/
src-tauri/plugins/*/android/.cxx/

# Firebase / FCM secrets — client config and the backend service-account key.
google-services.json
**/firebase-credentials.json

# A separate project checked out inside this repo — never commit it here.
/Freshon-farm-app/

# The Bruno API collection IS tracked. Nothing in it may carry a real
# credential or a real phone number: the collection-level bearer token and the
# login requests read {{deviceKey}} and {{phone}}, and prod.bru declares
# deviceKey/refreshToken/accessToken as `vars:secret`, which Bruno keeps in its
# local store rather than in the file. Fill them in your own environment.
